  "notes": [
   "This response is built from pages showing steps 1-7 of the booklet. The line drawings are small and ambiguous in places, so several placements are best guesses.",
   "Step 1: I read it as a yellow 1x2 plate (b2) at the end of the black 2x6 plate (b1). The picture could also show a larger yellow plate.",
   "Step 2: the black 2x4 brick (b3) sits over the rear of the plate and covers b2.",
   "Step 3: the yellow 2x3 plate (b4) goes on the front of the black plate. The yellow inverted slope 4x4 (b5) goes on the black brick.",
   "Step 4: the dark gray inverted slope (b6) goes at the front. I read the red arrows as two yellow 1x2 plates stacked on b5 (b7 on b5, b8 on b7).",
   "Step 5: I placed a yellow 2x4 plate (b9) over the cab area. The exact footprint is uncertain.",
   "Step 6: the dark gray ladder plate (b10) goes on the front. A yellow 1x3 brick (b11) goes beside it, with trans-clear round plates (b12, b13) as headlight studs.",
   "Step 7: the yellow wedge plate (b14) goes on top of the cab.",
   "other_joins is left empty because no pins, axles or clips appear in these steps. The wheels and wheel-holder plates are not in the steps shown, so none of them is placed here.",
   "Page 2 covers steps 8-12. The drawings are small, so exact positions are best guesses. Piece counts are consistent with the 33-piece inventory: pages 1 and 2 together use every piece.",
   "Step 8: the model is turned upside down. The two wheel-holder plates (b15, b16) clutch the underside of the black 2x6 plate (b1), one at each end.",
   "Step 9: the model is turned back over and the dump bed is built from two 1x4 bricks (b17, b18), a 1x3 brick (b19) and a 1x4 plate (b20). I read b17, b18 and b19 as sitting on the yellow inverted slope b5 and b20 on b18. The real arrangement may rest on more pieces.",
   "Step 10: a trans-clear 1x2 plate (b21) goes on the cab wedge (b14), with a yellow 1x2 plate (b22) on top of it, as the callout shows.",
   "Step 11: a yellow 2x4 plate (b23) goes across the bed bricks (b17, b18), with the two trans-red round plates (b24, b25) on it.",
   "Step 12: four wheels (b26-b29) go onto the wheel holders, two per holder plate. Each tyre (b30-b33) is fitted over its wheel. Tyres have no ports, so those edges carry no port names.",
   "The output schema has no rests_on field, so stud and clutch connections are given as joined edges with null ports. Each edge lists the piece placed first, then the piece it sits on.",
   "Step 3 of the first page had no edges. Those placements are not repeated here.",
   "The 14 separate groups were a real problem. My page 1 reply listed pieces b1-b14 but gave no connections between them. These new edges join them with stud connections, so together with the page 2 edges the whole truck is one connected assembly.",
   "Each edge lists the piece placed first, then the piece it sits on. The sitting-on relationships for b4, b6, b9, b10, b11, b12, b13 and b14 are best guesses from small drawings.",
   "Only additions are returned here: no new parts, and the earlier parts and page 2 edges stay unchanged."
  ]
 },
